note The edges. A call edge leaves level with the line that makes the call when that line is shown, and from the header otherwise, on a curve that leaves and enters horizontally and bows rightwards (direction 1.0) or leftwards (-1.0), reaching at least GRAPH_BEND of a column gap; a callee drawn to the left of its caller gets an orange curve from the caller's left side to the callee's right side instead of a wire across the canvas. Path edges, parent step to child step, are drawn last, thicker and green, and carry no label - the node's number is the label. A self-call and a callee that is already the caller's child step get no call edge.

